<title>BELGIUM: Finland will meet EMU criteria this year - Lipponen.</title>
<headline>Finland will meet EMU criteria this year - Lipponen.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Prime Minister Paavo Lipponen said on Wednesday his country would meet the criteria for Economic and Monetary Union this year.</p>
<p>Lipponen, on a visit to Brussels, told a news conference Finance Minister Sauli Niinisto had estimated Finland would meet all the criteria in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;So Finland, with Luxembourg, will be one of the two countries meeting ther criteria this year,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He said that after Italy joined the EU's exchange rate mechanism last weekend it was possible that a majority, perhaps eight to 10 countries, would be ready to join the third stage of EMU from the beginning in 1999.</p>
</text>
